quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  66,1,"O Prophet! Why do you prohibit (yourself from) what Allah has made lawful to you, (kindly) desiring the good pleasure of your wives? And Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  66,2,"(O believers!) Indeed, Allah has already ordained for you the (method of) absolution of your oaths. And Allah is your Guardian, and He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise."
  66,3,"And (remember) when the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him) had once said something secretly to one of his wives. But when she disclosed it (to another wife), and Allah made it known to him (blessings and peace be upon him), then he told (her) some part of it and held back the rest. So when he (blessings and peace be upon him) informed her of it, she said: ‘Who informed you about this?’ He (blessings and peace be upon him) said: ‘The All-Knowing, the All-Aware has informed me.’"
  66,4,"(It will be better) if you both repent to Allah because your hearts have inclined (together towards the same thing). But if you collaborate against him, Allah Himself is surely his Guardian, and are Jibril (Gabriel) and the righteous among the believers. Moreover, the angels are (also) his supporters."
  66,5,"It may be that if he divorces you, his Lord will give him wives better than yourselves. (They will also be) submissive, faithful, devoutly obedient, penitent, dedicated to worship and fasting, previously married and virgins."
  66,6,O believers! Protect yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is people and stones. It is overseen by severe and mighty angels who never disobey whatever Allah commands them and carry out what they are commanded (to do).
  66,7,(It will be said:) ‘O disbelievers! Do not make excuses today. You are only being repaid for what you used to do.’
